   "text": "This is a PROTAC-type molecule: a spirooxindole MDM2-binding unit joined through a benzamide and a four-carbon diamine linker to a thalidomide-type (pomalidomide-like) cereblon ligand.\n\n**Regions read from the drawing**\n- **Spirooxindole core:** a 6-chlorooxindole whose C3 is spiro-fused to a pyrrolidine. The pyrrolidine NH-adjacent carbon is itself spiro to a cyclohexane.\n- **Pyrrolidine substituents:** one carbon carries a 3-chloro-2-fluorophenyl group and the neighbouring carbon carries the carboxamide, whose N-aryl group is the central 1,4-phenylene.\n- **Linker:** the phenylene's para position carries a C(=O)NH\u2013(CH2)4\u2013NH\u2013C(=O)CH2\u2013O chain, counted as four CH2 units.\n- **Cereblon ligand:** the oxygen sits at position 4 of an isoindoline-1,3-dione, whose nitrogen is attached to a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl ring. That stereocentre is drawn with plain bonds, so I left it unspecified.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** there are three stereocentres with wedge or hash bonds.\n- The carboxamide-bearing carbon has a hashed bond to the carbonyl.\n- The aryl-bearing carbon has a wedge to the aryl group.\n- The oxindole spiro carbon has a wedge to the oxindole C=O.\n\nI assigned @/@@ from the 2D geometry by neighbour order. The spiro carbon on the cyclohexane is not a stereocentre, so it has no label.\n\nSMILES: O=C(NCCCCNC(=O)COc1cccc2c1C(=O)N(C1CCC(=O)NC1=O)C2=O)c1ccc(NC(=O)[C@@H]2NC3(CCCCC3)[C@@]4(C(=O)Nc5cc(Cl)ccc45)[C@H]2c2cccc(Cl)c2F)cc1"
